# Build output. `regenerate.sh` copies what the fixture needs out of it
# (`modules/*/module/*.wasm.zst` and the instrumented pair under
# `modules/*/page/`), so nothing here has to be committed.
modules/*/build/

# The instrumented modules are deliberately not committed in any form.
# They are only needed to *re-record*, and `regenerate.sh` builds them
# together with a fresh recording, so those two cannot drift apart the
# way the original module and the committed recording could. The repo
# root's blanket `*.wasm` already ignores them; this is the statement of
# intent.
modules/*/page/*.instrumented.wasm

# The ORIGINAL modules are committed as `modules/*/module/*.wasm.zst`.
#
# They are committed at all because they have to be *these* builds: the
# offline replay runs the ORIGINAL, uninstrumented module (spec §6.1) and
# checks every recorded crossing against it, so a module compiled by a
# different toolchain — with different export names, import indices or
# (for `vault_apply`) a different address for its `VAULT` block — no
# longer matches the recording.
#
# They are committed *compressed* because the repo caps a committed file
# at 500 KB and the raw modules are ~0.6 MB, almost entirely DWARF, which
# is the part the replay turns into per-line steps and locals and so
# cannot be stripped. `verify.sh` expands them into a temp directory.
